Description: Quantum Chimera validation test suites
 POSIX, client API and SMB test programs plus fio/elbencho benchmark
 configs installed under /opt/quantum/chimera/tests. The test programs
 run a Chimera stack in-process against a selectable VFS backend (-b),
 which lets a deployed system validate VFS modules such as SNFS without
 a development tree.
 .
 Also installs the caller-side chimera_vfs headers under
 /opt/quantum/chimera/tests/include, so a downstream in-process test
 fixture can build against the packaged libchimera_vfs.so rather than
 keeping its own copies of those declarations. They are chimera internals
 with no stability guarantee, unlike the module SDK in
 quantum-chimera-server, which is the supported boundary for an
 out-of-tree VFS backend. See tests/include/README for the include roots.
